  "refinements": [
    "Use actual public map with single-list and multi-list/rest/error/helper dependencies rather than unchecked primitive or handwritten toy",
    "Preserve source callback/read/recursive-return/cons ordering; input mutation is a stronger adversarial source-preservation envelope, explicitly not portable R7RS behavior",
    "Internal lexical functions may lift; user Scheme closure identity and captured mutable cells differ from captured continuation; stored artifact does not establish per-iteration closure allocation",
    "Unknown calls carry ProcRef/SELF/nargs/value protocol and explicit Scheme return frames; no fictional per-callback FFI wrapper saving",
    "Bounded dispatch host depth does not remove linear pending Scheme control; actual callback native/foreign domain remains separate",
    "Root custody spans entire suspended chain including prior callback results, current pair/proc, diagnostic arguments, dynamic state and code/frame users",
    "Multi-shot activation restores logical state and current allocation/owner binding without consuming unique native tokens or mutating earlier returned output",
    "Existing continuation capture/GC scan and wind/unwind sources require common frame/restore/decoder closure, not replacement by native defer or direct longjmp",
    "No-handles isolated output-cons B=3 remains conditional; unknown callback allocation has no whole-map bound; restricted logical source construction counts are not physical optimization lower bounds",
    "Existing mutable mismatch-policy default and signed helper sentinels remain runtime semantic dependencies; callback false/fixnum values are not tail sentinels",
    "Necessary call/frame product service decomposed into representation, validation, storage, cleanup, transfer/root, capture/lifetime and provider support after fair reuse",
    "Modern C is a funded reconstruction from current Gambit; include generator/validator/library/migration/delay/lifecycle cost and allow direct Zig delivery without prior C modernization",
    "Three cost ledgers distinguish C-versus-current, Zig-versus-current and incremental Zig-versus-fully-costed-C; common architecture does not imply equal or zero realization cost",
    "Ten handwritten implications, eighteen logical refuters, twelve unevaluated cases and three D2/SVG views; no checked proof, runtime witness, retirement or positive-net bound"
  ],
